	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44418</id><title>Peace Needs Children’s Voices</title><updated>2026-10-23T16:38:16-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44418" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/UN7559551______.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/UN7559551______.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/UN7559551______-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/UN7559551______.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
TOKYO, Japan, October 23 (IPS)  - WE THE PEOPLES OF THE UNITED NATIONS DETERMINED to save succeeding generations from the scourge of war, which twice in our lifetime has brought untold sorrow to mankind. The United Nations was established with this commitment.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44418&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Peace Needs Children’s Voices”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44419</id><title>Soil mapping aims to boost agricultural production in Kenya</title><updated>2026-10-23T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44419" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;A new Kenyan initiative is helping farmers better understand their soils in a bid to improve crop yields amid intensifying climate shocks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44419&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Soil mapping aims to boost agricultural production in Kenya”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44417</id><title>‘Burden and loss’ builds in DR Congo, as Kenya strengthens Ebola containment</title><updated>2026-10-23T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44417" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/25-09-2026_UNICEF_Ebola-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/25-09-2026_UNICEF_Ebola-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/25-09-2026_UNICEF_Ebola-01.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/25-09-2026_UNICEF_Ebola-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As Ebola continues to spread in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC), more resources are needed to fight the disease and feed patients and families, UN agencies said on Friday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44417&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “‘Burden and loss’ builds in DR Congo, as Kenya strengthens Ebola containment”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44416</id><title>Yemen: Deepening concerns for Taiz City as aid is blocked from entering</title><updated>2026-10-23T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44416" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/16-10-2026-WFP-Yemen-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/16-10-2026-WFP-Yemen-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/16-10-2026-WFP-Yemen-02.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/16-10-2026-WFP-Yemen-02.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Aid agencies warned on Friday of the fast-developing humanitarian emergency inside Taiz City in Yemen, which has been encircled by de facto Houthi forces fighting government troops along the country’s west coast.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44416&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Yemen: Deepening concerns for Taiz City as aid is blocked from entering”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44410</id><title>Were Half of Venezuela’s Oil Revenues Really Stolen? — Part II</title><updated>2026-10-23T04:58:29-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44410" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Barcos_en_Villa_Marina__.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Barcos_en_Villa_Marina__.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Barcos_en_Villa_Marina__-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Barcos_en_Villa_Marina__.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
DENVER, Colorado, USA, October 23 (IPS)  -  So, if Venezuela claims to be importing from the rest of the world roughly as much as it was exporting during those years, and the rest of the world confirms Venezuela’s story, then where could those additional $11 billion that presumably ended up in the bank accounts of Maduro’s cronies be?
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44410&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Were Half of Venezuela’s Oil Revenues Really Stolen? — Part II”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44411</id><title>The Eradication of Extreme Poverty by 2030: a Key UN goal will be a Missed Target</title><updated>2026-10-23T04:49:01-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44411" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/The-Eradication_630.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/The-Eradication_630.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/The-Eradication_630-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/The-Eradication_630.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
UNITED NATIONS, October 23 (IPS)  - The international day for the eradication of poverty, commemorated last week, was a grim reminder that the UN will not achieve its highly-ambitious target of helping eradicate extreme poverty—“in all its forms”– by 2030.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/23/44411&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “The Eradication of Extreme Poverty by 2030: a Key UN goal will be a Missed Target”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/22/44406</id><title>International Day of Climate Action 2026</title><updated>2026-10-22T06:52:56-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/22/44406" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/International-Day-of-Climate-Action-2026.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/International-Day-of-Climate-Action-2026.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/International-Day-of-Climate-Action-2026-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/International-Day-of-Climate-Action-2026.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
The world is getting hotter. And the consequences are already being felt. 
From devastating floods and prolonged droughts to intensifying heatwaves, climate change is disrupting lives and livelihoods across the globe.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/22/44406&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “International Day of Climate Action 2026”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/22/44405</id><title>Bangladesh’s Hidden Climate Bill: How Much Are We Losing Without Counting It?</title><updated>2026-10-22T05:49:53-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/22/44405" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Shahiduzzaman_200-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;
DHAKA, Bangladesh, October 22 (IPS)  - Bangladesh has earned global recognition for reducing deaths from cyclones and floods. Early warning systems, cyclone shelters, embankments and community preparedness have transformed the country’s disaster response. Yet another climate crisis is receiving far less attention: the economic damage climate change is quietly inflicting on households, farmers, workers, businesses and public finances.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/22/44405&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Bangladesh’s Hidden Climate Bill: How Much Are We Losing Without Counting It?”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/22/44415</id><title>First human case of Shamonda virus reported in France as patient dies</title><updated>2026-10-22T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/22/44415" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/31-09-2020-Unsplash-fossil-fuel-France.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/31-09-2020-Unsplash-fossil-fuel-France.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/31-09-2020-Unsplash-fossil-fuel-France.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/31-09-2020-Unsplash-fossil-fuel-France.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A patient in France has died after being infected with Shamonda virus, the first recorded human case of the disease.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/22/44415&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “First human case of Shamonda virus reported in France as patient dies”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/22/44414</id><title>Nepal’s deadly glacier flood a ‘defining moment’ for the international community</title><updated>2026-10-22T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/22/44414" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/28-08-2026-UNICEF-Nepal-floods-06.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/28-08-2026-UNICEF-Nepal-floods-06.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/28-08-2026-UNICEF-Nepal-floods-06.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/28-08-2026-UNICEF-Nepal-floods-06.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The deadly flash flood that tore through Nepal in August is a “defining moment” for both the country and the international community, according to the head of the UN field agency which builds roads, schools and clinics in crisis zones.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/22/44414&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Nepal’s deadly glacier flood a ‘defining moment’ for the international community”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry></feed><!-- 0.0057s ch:0 -->